# SCH-108 minimal public-entry owner packet

This is a local-only, unqualified candidate packet for root review.
source-head pins the exact implementation. base-head pins accepted schema 59.
The worktree is /root/lane-sch on ownsolid-cpu; product source remains offline.

- public-entry.md gives the actual constructor, signatures, trusted actor/
  audience/scope contract, routes and exact DTO.
- errors.md enumerates all eleven real module failures and separates IAM's
  pre-dispatch responsibilities.
- openapi.review.json is a review draft for DEV. It is not published, generated
  or a claim that production endpoints exist.
- ddl/ and ddl-dependencies.md give the exact two-table prerequisite, formal
  migration/catalog and native grant boundaries.
- authored-order and patches/ preserve every original author. Apply numerical
  patches with git am after inspecting the exact accepted base. The first six
  are retained scheduling prerequisites; the final three implement the
  quota-status reader, true owner error set and exact revision string.
- verification.md records pending commands and the precise lack of native
  qualification. It does not carry old test passes forward as new evidence.

IAM remains the trusted route owner, DEV the OpenAPI/SDK/Help owner and Web
the UI owner. ARC owns production DDL/catalog/grants and TRN owns its consumer.
This packet changes none of their production paths. No capacity/topology is
invented, and no roadmap item is ticked.
